+//! same per-chronon clamped 1/r^2 kick through `Kickable::kick`, same U/D marks at the
+//! same chronons) so the digest lineage is preserved; checkpoints at t=49152/98304 must
+//! reproduce c644's B/C counters and 19b9's contacts. The only new code is measurement:
+//!
+//! - `.core.tsv` per stride: population bands and contact/clamp shares.
+//!   Bands (raw units, Q = 2^20 = 1q): sub r<0.5q, q1 r<q, zone r<2.1q (9b3b's clamp
+//!   zone), near r<20q. `n_live` counts bodies not yet D-marked (r>250q).
+//!   ct_*_m = member contact-increments this stride (a pair inside the band counts 2).
+//! - `.body.tsv` per body at end: death/unbind/first-clamp times, min r ever, droplet
+//!   residence (strides with r<0.5q), first/last sub stride.
+//! - `.events.tsv`: beltewalk's `U`/`D` lines verbatim plus `F` at a body's first
+//!   clamped chronon.
